     words when no option is given is octal.

     The following options set the format of oodd's output:

     -bb   Dump bytes in the default base.

     -cc   Dump bytes as ASCII characters.  A printable byte is
          shown as a space and the character; a few control bytes
          are shown as a space and a backslash escape (\nn, \tt,
          and similarly for backspace, formfeed, carriage return,
          and NUL); any other byte falls back to the default
          base.

     -dd   Dump words in decimal.

     -oo   Dump words in octal.

     -xx   Dump words in hexadecimal.

